# Review authorities for diagnostic warrant reviews (Causal Warrant Gate V1.1).
#
# One line per authority:   <act:id> ed25519:<base64 public key>
#
# An authority enrols reviewers' keys (`lab-brain review enrol`); an answer to a warrant review
# counts only if it is signed with a key an authority listed here enrolled for that person in that
# project. This file is the trust anchor and lives OUTSIDE the database on purpose: whoever can
# write the database cannot make themselves an authority.
#
# THIS EXAMPLE PINS NO AUTHORITY, so no reviewer's answer verifies and every belief that needs a
# person waits (fail closed). To pin one:
#   1. the authority runs `lab-brain review keygen --out authority.key` on their own machine and
#      keeps the private key there;
#   2. the operator copies this file to `review-authorities` next to it (git-ignored), adds the
#      printed line, and points LAB_BRAIN_REVIEW_AUTHORITIES_FILE at it in `.env`;
#   3. `docker compose up` mounts it read-only into every service.
#
# act:pi ed25519:REPLACE_WITH_THE_AUTHORITY_PUBLIC_KEY
